---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/siteUrl';
import { CONTACTS } from '@varve/shared';
---

<Layout title="About Varve" description="Varve is built independently by one designer-developer: transparent development, honest limitations, and community input. Learn about the project, its FSL-1.1-MIT license, privacy, and security policies.">
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="about-page">
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">About Varve</h1>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Built in the open</h2>
        <p>
          Varve is developed independently, without VC pressure or corporate compromise. Development is transparent: architecture decisions, known limitations, and progress are documented publicly. Community input influences priorities. This independence means decisions are made for users rather than shareholders.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>The Vision</h2>
        <p>
          Design tools shouldn't require cloud subscriptions, data lock-in, or compromise on privacy. Varve is built on the belief that local-first architecture, native performance, and honest licensing can coexist with professional features and modern workflows.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Development Philosophy</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Technical depth over marketing fluff:</strong> Features are built when they work, not when they sound good in marketing copy</li>
          <li><strong>Honest limitations:</strong> What's not implemented is clearly labeled as "in development" or "types only"</li>
          <li><strong>Transparent roadmap:</strong> Public planning documents, open development process, community input on priorities</li>
          <li><strong>Quality gates:</strong> All changes must pass format, lint, typecheck, test, token audit, and emoji audit gates</li>
          <li><strong>Documentation-first:</strong> Architecture decisions, audits, and plans are documented as they're made</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>FSL-1.1-MIT Licensing</h2>
        <p>
          Varve is licensed under the <strong>Functional Source License, Version 1.1, MIT Future License</strong> (FSL-1.1-MIT). The source code is publicly available. FSL-1.1-MIT allows free use, modification, and redistribution for any Permitted Purpose — everything other than a Competing Use, such as offering a substitute product or service. Commercial redistribution as a competing product or hosted service requires a separate licence.
        </p>
        <p>
          After two years from each release, that release's code automatically converts to the MIT licence. This ensures that if the project ever ceases development, the code becomes fully open-source.
        </p>
        <a href={sitePath('/about/license')} class="btn-secondary">Read the full license</a>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Support the Project</h2>
        <p>
          As an independently developed project, Varve relies on community support to continue development. Financial support enables platform support, stability work, and features that might otherwise be deferred. Non-financial contributions — testing, documentation, design, translations — are equally valuable.
        </p>
        <a href={sitePath('/support-project')} class="btn-primary">Support the Project</a>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>
          Varve does not track users across sites or require cloud accounts. Optional website
          analytics is consent-based, uses no cookies or fingerprinting, and is disabled unless a
          production deployment explicitly configures it. The application keeps design data local.
        </p>
        <a href={sitePath('/about/privacy')} class="btn-secondary">Read the privacy policy</a>
      </section>

      <section class="about-section">
        <h2>Security Policy</h2>
        <p>
           Security vulnerabilities can be reported privately via GitHub Private Vulnerability Reporting or
           <a href={`mailto:${CONTACTS.security}`}>{CONTACTS.security}</a>. The project follows coordinated disclosure practices.
        </p>
        <a href={sitePath('/security')} class="btn-secondary">Read the security policy</a>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .about-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }
  
  .about-page .page-hero-title {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  
  .about-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  
  .about-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  
  .about-section p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  
  .about-section ul {
    list-style: none;
  }
  
  .about-section li {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }
  
  .about-section li::before {
    content: "•";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--text-link-hover);
    font-weight: bold;
  }
  
  .about-section strong {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .about-page h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
  }
</style>
